course: dictionary
lesson: 1442
title: Carry: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so you must check the words around it to know which one is meant. The word carry is a good example. «The bus carries 40 people.» Here carry means the bus can hold or take a load of 40 people. Check it by swapping in hold: the bus can hold 40 people, so the meaning works.
explain: Look at the words next to carry. «Never carry packages or bags for strangers.» Here carry means to hold something and take it with you. The clue is packages and bags, which are things you hold and move.
explain: Some meanings are in phrases, so look at the whole phrase. «If you lose your place, staying calm and carrying on usually works.» Carrying on means keeping going. Carry on is a phrase, so it means something different from carry alone.
explain: In maths, carry has a special meaning. In adding, to carry is to move a ten to the next place. Each time you see carry, ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Carry means to hold something and take it with you.
fact: «The bus carries 40 people» means the bus can hold or take that many people.
fact: In adding, to carry means to move a ten to the next place.
fact: «Carry on» means keep going, and «carry out» means do.
fact: In science, blood carries oxygen around the body.
exercise: «Never carry packages or bags for strangers.» What does carry mean here? | To move a ten to the next place | * To hold and take with you | To keep going | To be able to hold a load of 40
exercise: «If you lose your place, staying calm and carrying on usually works.» What does carrying on mean? | Holding a bag | * Keeping going | Moving a ten | Shouting loudly
exercise: In adding 38 + 25, the ones make 13, so you write 3 and do what with the ten? | Multiply it by two | Throw it away | * Carry it to the next place | Turn it into a word
test: «Marsupials, such as kangaroos and koalas, carry their tiny newborns in a pouch.» What does carry mean here? | To move a ten to the next place | * To hold and take with you | To keep going | To cheer for
test: «Gulls have learned that people carry food.» Which meaning fits best? | To be quiet | To add a ten | * To hold and take with you | To keep going, like carry on
exam: In «The bus carries 40 people», what does carries mean? | To hold or take a load | * To hold or take a load, as in a bus that can take 40 people | To drop slowly | To shout
